<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54051" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταιδέομαι</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έσομαι</span>: aor.
		
			Pass.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῃδέσθην</span> in act. sense:—
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>feel shame</i> or
				<i>reverence before</i> another, <i>stand in awe of</i> him,
			c. acc., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.72
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				654
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				682
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμονα καταιδεσθεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					772
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταιδέσθητι πατρῷον Δία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					1468
				</span></i>
			 (paratrag.): c. inf., <i>to be ashamed to
			do</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				1027
			</span></i>: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				805
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				38.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later in 
				Act.
			, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταιδέω</span></b> ,
				<i>put to shame</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				4.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				15.191b
			</span></i>, f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.801f
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i></div>
